    "about": {
      "title": "About Me",
      "data": "I'm a software architect based in Guadalajara. I've spent seven years building and fixing .NET systems — from old .NET Framework 2.0 apps to .NET 10 and 11 — and I like the part most people avoid: understanding legacy code well enough to change it safely.\n\nI've worked with AI every day for the last four years, from ChatGPT to Codex, Claude Code and Antigravity. I treat it like a fast teammate whose work still needs a review, so I build my own MCP servers and guardrails to keep it honest.\n\nI care about clear designs, realistic estimates and code the next person can pick up without having to call me."
    },
